Sval: hide File's last line with Quit on macOS

Sval's menu bar takes out Work Offline, which stood between File's last
line and Quit. macOS takes Quit out of File and hides the line above it
only by this id (`nsMenuBarX::AquifyMenuBar`), so without it File ends
on a line there.

diff --git a/browser/base/content/browser-menubar.inc.xhtml b/browser/base/content/browser-menubar.inc.xhtml
index 0ee46612bd..d8c4a5c727 100644
--- a/browser/base/content/browser-menubar.inc.xhtml
+++ b/browser/base/content/browser-menubar.inc.xhtml
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
                 <menuseparator/>
                 <menuitem id="menu_importFromAnotherBrowser"
                           command="cmd_file_importFromAnotherBrowser" data-l10n-id="menu-file-import-from-another-browser"/>
-                <menuseparator/>
+                <menuseparator id="menu_FileQuitSeparator"/>
                 <menuitem id="menu_FileQuitItem"
 #ifdef XP_MACOSX
                           data-l10n-id="menu-quit-mac"
